WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.850
At one national retail and hospitality chain, a rostering app keeps a fairness-credit tally of each worker's weekend shifts.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.180
At six in a rolling eight weeks,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.270
it stops offering them weekend shifts.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.260
And nothing in its rules touches a worker's appraisal.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.114
A paper from the School of Emergent Priorities asks whether it does anyway.

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:23.901
When a worker crosses that line,

00:00:24.001 --> 00:00:26.581
does their supervisor describe them differently?

00:00:27.481 --> 00:00:31.261
A worker one shift either side of the line is much the same worker.

00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:35.581
So we followed four hundred and thirty-eight casual and part-time staff,

00:00:35.681 --> 00:00:37.411
at twenty-four outlets.

00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:45.231
The team searched each worker's next appraisal for words like flexible, adaptable, and easy to roster around.

00:00:46.131 --> 00:00:49.241
Just under the threshold, fifty-eight per cent of appraisals used one.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:50.941
Over it, only twenty-two.

00:00:51.341 --> 00:00:53.571
That's a fall of thirty-six points, and it stayed down.

00:00:54.871 --> 00:00:57.771
We also checked the things the threshold ought to move.

00:00:58.371 --> 00:01:01.250
Rostered hours, shift swaps, logged incidents.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.280
None of them move.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.490
Only the words do.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:09.510
As a check, three placebo cutoffs, where the app enforces nothing, show no such jump.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.260
The chain has already seen an early version of our results.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:19.130
It now proposes filling in each draft appraisal with a flexibility rating,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.920
worked out from the same tally.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.600
A threshold built to even out the weekend roster has ended up deciding what a supervisor writes down,

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.020
and the worker never sees either number.
